  "notes": "Presco Plc \u2014 Nigerian Stock Exchange listed integrated palm oil producer. Owns ~40,000 ha (~99k acres) of oil palm plantations + extraction mills + refinery in Edo / Delta States. Acquired Saro Oil Palm Company (~14k ha) and Ghana Oil Palm Development Co. (GOPDC) stake during FY2023-2024. Calendar fiscal year. NGN reporting; figures in NGN millions. FY2023-2024 results reflect significant boost from Naira devaluation (NGN-denominated CPO realised prices tracked global USD prices). Ramp in revenue/EBITDA from FY2022 onwards reflects both Naira devaluation (NGN/USD ~415 in 2022 \u2192 ~1,500 in 2024) and palm-oil price strength. Land book reflects revaluation gains. Acres ~99k (40k ha). Net debt swung positive from FY2023 due to Saro / GOPDC acquisitions financed by debt. Pre-FY2022 financials reflect a much smaller business (only Presco core ~20k ha) and pre-devaluation exchange rates.",
